        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2016 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "For secundum ASD, a deficient retro-aortic rim is common (40% of cases) However, the deficient retro-aortic rim had no effect on ASD device placement success or immediate outcome The IMPACT Registry does not track long-term outcome, so there is no information provided about long-term complications, such as erosion."
